WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.637
The word supervised means that the training examples include the correct target.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:11.977
During training, the model receives X, the feature matrix, and y, the known target values.

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:17.017
The algorithm uses those labeled examples to estimate model parameters.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:22.423
After training, the fitted model receives a new feature vector and produces a prediction.

00:00:23.226 --> 00:00:26.283
This sequence is central to supervised learning.

00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:28.818
Known examples teach the model.

00:00:28.818 --> 00:00:33.108
New cases test whether the learned pattern generalizes.

00:00:33.108 --> 00:00:37.698
You will see this same pattern with many algorithms next semester.

00:00:37.698 --> 00:00:45.648
The internal mathematics may be different, but the workflow remains recognizable: collect labeled examples,

00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:53.789
represent them numerically, fit the model, evaluate on unseen data, and then use the model for new predictions.
